{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1045019-question-about-yantra","id":1045019,"title":"Question about Yantra.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-07T06:25:18-08:00","id":1045019,"title":"Question about Yantra.","content":"Hello everyone, i'll start by saying English ain't the primary language in our game, yet the book are in english, so sometime confusion on translation can happen.<br /> <br /> The question come directly from this fact. we all pretty much understand english quite decently, some better then other but that's not really important, the storyteller is the only one having the core rulebook (even though he shared the pdf format with us). I generally am better then he is with english, but since he is the storyteller, he usually get to make the call wheter something is oki or not and we're all fine with this. He sometime ask me to check some rules for him so we can better understand everything.<br /> <br /> We've been playing for around 5 session now with the new edition (wich we converted our old character to, so they are not really newbie). Recently i was checking something to prepare a rote I was about to make when I read again about yantra and to my understanding, it would clash from what our storyteller understood and explained to us.<br /> <br /> Basically, from what he explained to us, is that Yantra can give you a maximum of +5 dice (all yantra combined) so for our character with gnosis 5, many skill at 4-5 and our sphere at 3-4, when using rote and getting skill mudra, it's quite often we only use our skill mudra as yantra since with his explanation, we can't go any higher then this.<br /> <br /> However, after reading the ruling, my understanding would be somewhat different, sure you can't gain more then +5 BUT these come AFTER the penalty are taken into account (wich to me would include dice removed to augment potency, duration or scale) wich would then change the way we use yantra, instead of only going for 1 yantra wich cap us at +5, we could incorporate more yantra to offset the diced removed from said augmentation like High speech, shadow name, environmental yantra and such.<br /> <br /> So the question would then be, wich of our understanding would be right, mine or his?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:31:57-08:00","id":1045027,"title":"","content":"You are correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:17:19-08:00","id":1045045,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick answer and sorry for my poor english <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:19:17-08:00","id":1045046,"title":"","content":"You are correct, however remember that each Yantras after the first adds a round to the casting time. This can be deviating during battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:38:47-08:00","id":1045052,"title":"","content":"I guess we are lucky, we aren't going into battle quite often, but when we do, we rarely go with multiple yantra mainly for that reason, High Speech and concentration are often left aside aswell, but already with these, going for 7-8 lethal damage attack (aggravated sometimes when we don't care about the paradox biting us) fight tend to resolve rather quickly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}